      "documentConcept": "Spinal cord stimulation, TMS and tDCS for gait and motor symptoms",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:32751397857cf61158808007104df095460896d2d57de12980c4571df7983c69",
      "text": "Spinal cord and noninvasive cortical stimulation are being studied for Parkinson gait and motor symptoms. Two blinded SCS trials did not establish gait benefit from the tested protocols, while an open extension suggested improvements that require controlled confirmation. rTMS trials and pooled analyses report improvements in selected freezing, gait-speed, and motor outcomes, with important limits from small samples and protocol variation. tDCS has mixed secondary signals but a negative primary freezing trial and insufficient pooled motor evidence. Claims below distinguish primary outcomes, secondary findings, open extensions, and procedural or stimulation adverse effects.",
